# Milestone: M3
# Covers: ambient tag chain is inherited by strands spawned via the `,`
#         (fork-detach) separator; tag.stop() on the ambient tag cascades to
#         the parallel strand (row 11 §4.3 + T38 separator runtime).
#
# blocked: top-level & separator hangs chk driver — T39 chk-runner urbi_step driver path (audit Cat. A)
# matrix-row: tag-ambient
#
# Reason: the `,` separator runtime (OP_FORK_DETACH) is not yet wired at M3;
# T38 activates that opcode.  Additionally, tag.stop() method-call syntax
# requires M4 object model.  Both must land before this fixture is active.
#
# When T38 + M4 land, implement this fixture by uncommenting the source below.
# Expected behaviour: the spawned inner strand is a member of `t` and is
# stopped when t.stop() fires.  "inner done" must NOT appear in output.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T38 + M4):
#   var t = Tag.new;
#   var log = "";
#   t: { log = log + "outer", { log = log + "inner" | t.stop() } };
#   log
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] "outer"
